@tool
class_name Controls

# every button binding of the game and its tools, in one table. an entry is
#   {group, description, keys, mouse, joy, physical, builtin}
# keys are Key codes with KEY_MASK_* modifiers or'd in (KEY_MASK_CMD_OR_CTRL
# is Ctrl, Cmd on macOS), mouse are MouseButton indices, also with modifier
# masks or'd in, joy are JoyButton indices. physical entries bind the key
# position (WASD stays WASD on AZERTY), the rest bind the key label.
# builtin entries are Godot's own ui_* actions the menus lean on, listed
# here so the controls list is complete, never registered or written out.
#
# the table is the source of truth. register() adds what is missing to the
# InputMap at startup (GameSettings._ready), project.godot's [input] section
# is generated from it by GenerateInputMap.gd and a test checks the two
# agree, docs/CONTROLS.md is generated by GenerateControlsDoc.gd, and the
# pause menu and the F3 panel list describe(). scripts never test raw keys
# or buttons: game code asks event.is_action_pressed(Controls.X) or
# Input.is_action_pressed(Controls.X), the editors and plugins that also run
# inside the Godot editor (whose InputMap does not carry the game's actions)
# ask pressed / released / matches / held here, which fall back to the
# table, and editor buttons can take shortcut(action).
#
# modifiers when matching an event: Shift and Alt on the event are ignored
# unless the binding asks for them, Ctrl is not, so B and Ctrl+B are
# different bindings (Cmd counts as Ctrl)

